# Music. Not ours to redistribute, and a single WAV master is bigger than the
# rest of the repo put together. The folder structure matters; the audio does
# not travel with the code.
# The show folders are not tracked at all — start.sh creates them from
# schedule.json on every run. Keeping them with .gitkeep placeholders looks
# tidier and breaks the station: Liquidsoap's playlist retries the rejected
# placeholder forever instead of treating the folder as empty.
# Only the show subfolders (the audio), not music/ itself — CREDITS.md and
# the prompt sheets are small text and worth keeping in history.
music/*/
drops/today/
retired/

# Original recordings, renders and mockups — large binaries that would bloat
# history. Keep them backed up somewhere that isn't git.
sources/

# Raw AI-generated candidates and voice takes, pre-selection. What actually
# makes air lives in music/ and drops/today/ (also untracked) or, for the
# web samples, in web/samples/ (tracked). This folder is the working pile.
trials/
Audio_recorded/

# Generated at runtime. logs/icecast.xml in particular is built from the
# password in station.liq, so committing it would publish that password.
logs/
nowplaying.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
